# Postman collection

`apps/api/postman/umc-api.postman_collection.json` (Postman v2.1) must always match the API. The environment file `umc-local.postman_environment.json` holds `baseUrl`, `email`, `password`.

## When to update

Update the collection **in the same change** whenever you:

- add, remove, or rename an endpoint (route, method, or path in `API_ROUTES`);
- change a request body, query params, or path params (validator / shared request type);
- change auth/role requirements, status codes, or response shape worth documenting.

## How

- One folder per feature (`Users`, `Clients`, …), ordered as mounted in `routes/index.ts`.
- URLs: `{{baseUrl}}/<path>` with both `raw` and `path` segments filled in; ids as `{{<feature>Id}}`.
- Auth is inherited from the collection (Bearer `{{accessToken}}`). Public endpoints (health, login/refresh/logout) set `"auth": { "type": "noauth" }`.
- Bodies: realistic sample JSON covering every field the Zod schema accepts, valid enum values only.
- List requests: `page`/`pageSize` enabled, every other filter present but `"disabled": true`, with allowed values in `description`.
- Create requests get a test script that saves `res.data.id` into the matching collection variable; declare that variable in the top-level `variable` array.
- Put role requirements on the folder `description`, and non-obvious behaviour (204, at-least-one-field PATCH) on the request.
- Never commit real values: `accessToken`, ids, `email` and `password` stay `""`.
- Run `npx prettier --write apps/api/postman` and make sure the file is still valid JSON.

```json
{
  "name": "Get client",
  "request": {
    "method": "GET",
    "header": [],
    "url": {
      "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/clients/{{clientId}}",
      "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
      "path": ["clients", "{{clientId}}"]
    }
  }
}
```
